---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import TldrBox from '../../components/TldrBox.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = "/for/fashion";
const title = "Shopify SMS apps for fashion: drops, sizes and returns";
const desc = "Compare fashion SMS candidates with variant-level drop checks, returns suppression, seasonal permissions and a margin-based pilot.";
const faqs = [{"question": "Which app is best for a fashion drop?", "answer": "Shortlist Postscript, Attentive, Klaviyo or Omnisend according to your existing data and team. Require a demonstration of size-level availability, purchase exits and returns handling before choosing; this page reports no comparative performance test."}, {"question": "Should a return trigger a winback text?", "answer": "Pause related promotion while the return or exchange is unresolved. Resume only when the order state, message purpose and channel permission support it."}, {"question": "Do I need separate email and SMS vendors?", "answer": "No. Several candidates offer both channels. Compare the coordination and total cost of one platform against any benefit from separate vendors."}];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a href="/for" class="link">← All store types</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9">A collection launch is only useful to a shopper when the linked size and colour are available. Evaluate messaging tools against that inventory problem before adding more broadcasts.</p>
    <p class="mt-5">A workflow guide, not a tested ranking. Product scope checked November 25, 2026; confirm account availability and current terms before purchase.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <TldrBox title="Candidates by evaluation task" picks={[{"label": "Shopify campaigns", "tool": "Postscript", "reason": "Evaluate drop audiences and inventory handoffs; its current offer also includes Email."}, {"label": "Regional programs", "tool": "Attentive", "reason": "Compare email and SMS coordination across the destinations you serve."}, {"label": "Shared customer data", "tool": "Klaviyo", "reason": "Evaluate separate channel permissions and purchase-based segments."}, {"label": "Combined messaging", "tool": "Omnisend", "reason": "Compare email, SMS and web push workflows without assuming all three are needed."}]} />
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Start with the garment and variant</h2>
      <p>Keep product ID, variant ID, size, colour, available inventory and destination URL in the launch brief. A product being in stock does not mean the subscriber’s size is available. Ask each candidate to demonstrate the exact event and filter combination in your store; a general Shopify integration is not proof of variant-aware suppression.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Proposed drop rehearsal: inventory changes before send</h2>
      <p>This is a proposed fixture, not an observed merchant test. Create consenting test profiles for two sizes, a sold-out size, a recent purchaser and an opted-out contact. Queue a drop, then sell out one variant before release. Check whether the queued audience is re-evaluated, which landing page opens, and how the team cancels a stale message. Do not announce a sell-through percentage unless live inventory supports it.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Returns and exchanges change the next message</h2>
      <p>A return request should pause the related promotional sequence while service resolves the order. An exchange into another size should update the next recommendation rather than restart cart recovery for the original size. Verify which return, refund and cancellation events your integration actually receives, their delay, and the fallback when the returns app does not sync them. Keep order-service communication separate from marketing preferences.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Seasonal permission is narrower than permanent interest</h2>
      <p>A winter-coat waitlist or a one-off event signup does not establish interest in every future collection. Store the capture wording and source beside channel permission. Offer a preference path for collection interest and reassess dormant seasonal audiences before the next launch. Let shoppers leave marketing without losing access to necessary order updates; verify the applicable rules for each destination with qualified advice.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Compare candidates on the same fashion workflow</h2>
      <p>Postscript is a candidate for Shopify campaign execution, and its current platform includes Email; a separate email tool is not mandatory. Attentive supports email and SMS programs across supported regions. Klaviyo documents separate email and SMS lists and purchase-related segments. Omnisend offers email, SMS and web push. These capabilities justify a shortlist, not a winner: ask each team to demonstrate size availability, returns exits and duplicate-message prevention using your actual integrations.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Email alternatives and current product boundaries</h2>
      <p>Sequenzy documents Shopify customer, order and product sync plus purchase-based email workflows; its optional SMS add-on means it should not be described as email-only. Evaluate whether its events and destination support fit your drop workflow. Drip’s August–September 2026 release notes introduce Drip SMS, so older email-only comparisons need rechecking. Yotpo retired Email & SMS on December 31, 2025; Reviews and Loyalty are separate products. Firepush’s November 2026 article notice says it now offers web push rather than email or SMS campaigns.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Measure retained margin after the return window</h2>
      <p>For a proposed pilot, randomize eligible shoppers into message and holdout groups before sending. Compare net revenue per eligible shopper after refunds, then subtract goods, fulfillment, return handling, incentives and messaging costs on a consistent basis. Include unsent eligible shoppers in the denominator. Do not count a discount twice if net revenue already reflects it. Wait for a suitable return window; attributed orders alone do not establish incremental profit.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Before releasing a collection</h2>
      <p>Assign one owner to approve inventory truth, offer expiry, size links and the combined channel calendar. Keep channel-specific consent, suppression and recipient-time scheduling intact during migration. Test opt-out handling and purchase exits. Obtain a current quote for the same destination mix, message encoding, peak audience and required integrations; no revenue threshold on its own determines the right plan.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Primary sources for product scope</h2>
      <p><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript channels</a>; <a class="link" href="https://help.attentive.com/hc/en-us/articles/16948569849492-Send-messages-internationally-with-Attentive">Attentive destinations</a>; <a class="link" href="https://help.klaviyo.com/hc/en-us/articles/360024538231">Klaviyo segments</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.omnisend.com/">Omnisend channels</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/features/shopify-integration">Sequenzy Shopify integration</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.sequenzy.com/best-sms-marketing-tools-for-small-business">Sequenzy SMS scope</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.drip.com/release-notes/august-september-2026">Drip SMS release</a>; <a class="link" href="https://www.yotpo.com/blog/email-sms-migration-partners/">Yotpo retirement notice</a>; <a class="link" href="https://getfirepush.com/blog/targeted-email-marketing/">Firepush current notice</a>.</p>
      <p><a class="link" href="/apps">Browse app profiles</a> or <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">plan campaign restraint</a>. Recheck any linked guide against your current destination requirements.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
